CORE
main.bash

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.1\] file main.bash line 4 assertion "\$\{\?\}" -eq 0: FAILURE$
^\[assertion\.2\] file main.bash line 6 assertion "\$\{\?\}" -eq 0: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
As verify-redirection-failure, but bash (outside POSIX mode) does not
exit when a redirection of a special builtin fails.
